  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>The Palmerston Hotel is in the directories in <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> from 1867 to 1905. It is No. 97 from 1869 to 1885, No. 127 in 1890 and No. 135 from 1895.</p>
        <p>The directories list the proprietors as Robert Ure (1867), Patrick Rafferty (1868 to 1876, also printed Raffarty), J. Raftery (1877), James Heaney (1878), Thomas F. Buxton (1879 to 1885), Thomas Reece (1890), John O'Connor (1895), Mrs H. King (1900) and Mrs M. Matthew (1905).</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>John Dunning's wood yard is next to the hotel in 1867 and 1868. In 1879 Edward Noel Gerard, artist and modeller, is listed beside it.</p>
      </div>
